Recover after a simulated lost acknowledgment — learner brief
Fictional Northstar Services training material.
Failure
A/B/C September. Fail once after B effect is durably recorded before acknowledgment; stop before C. Recovery reads ledger; one recovery pass. D lacks period and must be rejected without retry.
Task
The routine writes a draft entry but fails before returning success. Demonstrate that recovery does not repeat the effect.
Actions
	1	Mark the failure point in the sequence: effect recorded, acknowledgment absent.
	2	Run the injected-failure scenario and inspect which effects exist.
	3	Ask AI for a recovery path that reads the ledger before creating effects.
	4	Recover B as already completed and process C; reject invalid D without retry.
	5	Confirm A, B, and C each have one effect and write an operator instruction for an unresolved failure.
Output
Failure point; before/after ledger; recovery attempts; rejected item; operator instruction.
Supplied local practice files
	•	failure.json
	•	ledger.py
	•	replay.json
Keep these files together. Scripts take explicit paths; choose new output folders. Use a plain text editor to inspect source before running. Browser prototypes open locally; do not deploy them.
